    "result_text": "The build passes with the single test (`coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`) green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n`membershipTier` now resolves to `GOLD` when the owner's household has 3+ members after the create, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply. I followed the exact pattern already established for `namesakeCount` (compute at create time \u2192 persist a snapshot \u2192 resolve tier in the mapper), so no class became a catch-all and existing logic was reused rather than duplicated:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (the generated `MembershipTierEnum` previously only had BRONZE/SILVER) and updated its description.\n2. **Schema (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`)** \u2014 added a `household_size INTEGER` column alongside `namesake_count`.\n3. **`Owner`** \u2014 added the persisted `householdSize` field with getter/setter.\n4. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `countHouseholdMembers(lastName, address)`, a read-only method returning the household size after this create (existing members via the existing `findHouseholdMembers` helper, plus the new owner). No new query logic \u2014 it reuses the same last-name + canonical-address matching that `assignHousehold`/`existsOwnerInHousehold` already use.\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` at create time, next to the existing `namesakeCount` assignment.\n6. **`OwnerMapper.resolveMembershipTier`** \u2014 GOLD takes precedence when `householdSize >= 3` (named constant `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE`), otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\nBecause the tier is a per-owner snapshot (\"3+ members **after this create**\"), persisting `householdSize` at creation matches the spec's semantics and survives the re-fetch that `getOwner` does before mapping.",
